        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c=10$.",
          "worked": "The y-intercept is c. Setting $y=0$ gives the x-intercept $\\frac{c}{5}$. Hence $$\\begin{aligned}\\frac12\\times c\\times\\frac c5&=10\\\\c^2&=100\\\\c&=10\\end{aligned}$$ because c is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
